# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Local configuration that may name hosts or carry an allowlist.
# Nothing secret should ever live here -- capability comes from the process
# environment, never from a file -- but a host-specific config is still noise
# in a shared repo.
config.local.json

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Generated semantic indexes. Rebuildable with `vault_index.py build`, and
# several MB of float vectors apiece -- a build artefact, not source. The
# vectors are also only valid for the embedding model and prefixes that made
# them, so a committed index goes stale invisibly. An index also contains the
# text of everything it indexed, so committing one publishes the corpus.
#
# Scoped to the repo root, not `**`, so that example or fixture JSON in a
# subdirectory is still trackable rather than silently disappearing.
#
# ⚠️ BUT IT SWALLOWS ANY ROOT-LEVEL JSON, SILENTLY. On 2026-08-30 a verification
# register written to the repo root was invisible to `git status` and nothing
# said so -- `git check-ignore -v <file>` is what found it. Before adding any
# root-level .json, run that. Anything meant to be tracked belongs in a
# subdirectory or needs an explicit negation below.
/*.json
# A built index contains the corpus, verbatim, in its chunk text. `/*.json`
# only covers the repository root; an index directory pointed anywhere inside
# the tree by OLLAMA_MCP_INDEX_DIR would slip past it.
*.index.json
# The skill ZIP the README builds for upload -- a build product, not source
/*.zip

# Built by ci/build_skill_zip.py
/dist/
